<div class="qhx-page">
<nav class="crumb wrap" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>About Our Academy</span>
</nav>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow-plain">About Our Academy</p>
    <h1>The academy behind the home of Quran learning</h1>
    <p class="lede">QuranlyHub exists for one reason: to give Muslim families in the UK, USA, Canada, Australia, UAE, Qatar and Saudi Arabia a Quran education they can trust — certified, one-to-one, and built around real family schedules.</p>
</div>
</header>

<section>
  <div class="wrap grid-2">
    <div>
      <h2>Why we built QuranlyHub</h2>
<img width="800" height="649" src="https://quranlyhub.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/about-learning-environment.webp" class="attachment-large size-large" alt="About: online learning environment" style="border-radius:14px;max-width:100%;height:auto;margin:24px 0 0;display:block;" decoding="async" />
      <p>Most families searching for an <strong>online Quran academy</strong> run into the same two problems. Either they land in an overcrowded group class, where a child gets a few minutes of real attention in a 45-minute session — or they hire an unverified freelance tutor with no consistent curriculum, no accountability, and no way to check credentials.</p>
      <p>QuranlyHub was built as the alternative: a proper academy, not a marketplace. Every tutor on our platform holds a verified Ijazah — a formal certification in Quranic recitation passed down through an unbroken chain of teachers — and every class is taught one-to-one, live over video, following a structured course rather than an improvised lesson plan.</p>
      <p>We serve families across seven countries — the United Kingdom, United States, Canada, Australia, United Arab Emirates, Qatar and Saudi Arabia — which means our tutors teach around the clock, across every time zone, so a class in Manchester at 5pm and a class in Sydney at 7am can both happen without either family compromising.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="principle"><h3>Certified, not self-declared</h3><p>Every tutor's Ijazah is verified before they teach a single student — we don't rely on a tutor's word for their own qualification.</p></div>
      <div class="principle"><h3>One student, one tutor</h3><p>No shared class slots. Your child or you are the only student in the room for the full 30 minutes, every session.</p></div>
      <div class="principle"><h3>A curriculum, not a playlist</h3><p>Courses progress in a fixed order — Qaida, then Tajweed, then Hifz or Tafseer — so progress is measurable, not incidental.</p></div>
      <div class="principle"><h3>Built for real family life</h3><p>24/7 scheduling and flexible rebooking mean Quran learning fits around school, work and prayer times — not the other way round.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="alt">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Our mission</h2>
    <p>To be the home of Quran learning for every Muslim family — wherever they live, whatever their schedule — by pairing them with a certified, dedicated tutor and a clear path from their first Arabic letter to confident recitation, memorisation and understanding.</p>
    <p>We measure success the way a parent does: not in enrolment numbers, but in whether a child looks forward to their next class, and whether an adult who started Qaida at 35 can, a year later, read Quran online with confidence they didn't have before.</p>
    <p>That same standard applies whether a family is booking a single 30-minute Noorani Qaida session or committing to the multi-year Alim &amp; Aalimah path, the tutor, the one-to-one attention and the free trial before any commitment stay exactly the same.</p> <p>We built it this way deliberately: a family shouldn't have to compare five different platforms to figure out which one is trustworthy, they should be able to come to one academy and know every tutor meets the same bar, whatever course or country they happen to be teaching from.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap grid-2">
    <div>
      <h2>How a family joins QuranlyHub</h2>
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="step"><h3>1. Book a free trial</h3><p>No credit card, no commitment — just a short form so we understand the student's age, level and goals.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><h3>2. Meet a matched tutor</h3><p>A live evaluation call pairs the student with a tutor suited to their level — including a female tutor on request, arranged via WhatsApp before the trial.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><h3>3. Start the right course</h3><p>Whether that's Noorani Qaida for a first-time reader or Advanced Tajweed for a returning student, the course — and price — stay consistent from day one.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Our courses</h2>
      <p style="margin-top:-8px;">Every course below is taught 1-on-1 by an Ijazah-certified tutor, at one consistent monthly price.</p>
      <nav class="course-strip" aria-label="QuranlyHub courses">
        <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/noorani-qaida/">Noorani Qaida <span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/quran-reading-tajweed/">Quran Reading with Tajweed <span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/quran-memorization-hifz/">Quran Memorization (Hifz) <span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/tafseer/">Tafseer-ul-Quran <span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/advanced-tajweed/">Advanced Tajweed Course <span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/quranic-arabic/">Quranic Arabic Course <span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/alim-aalimah-course/">Alim &amp; Aalimah Course <span class="go">→</span></a>
      </nav>
      <p style="margin-top:18px;"><a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/">See our full course catalogue →</a></p>
    <p style="margin-top:14px;">Our newest addition is the <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/services/alim-aalimah-course/">Alim &amp; Aalimah course</a>, a full path to becoming a certified Islamic scholar rather than a single subject. It brings Quran recitation and Tajweed, Tafseer, Hadith, Fiqh and Arabic together under one tutor relationship instead of six separate enrolments, with a female tutor available throughout for sisters on the Aalimah track. Because QuranlyHub is Pakistan-based, we're also able to teach it, and Tafseer specifically, in Urdu as well as English, which is one of the reasons families choose us over academies that only operate in one language.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Where our families learn from</h2>
    <p class="narrow">QuranlyHub schedules classes 24/7 to serve Muslim families across seven countries. Explore Quran classes local to you:</p>
    <nav class="course-strip" aria-label="QuranlyHub locations" style="margin-top:22px;">
      <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/locations/uk/">Online Quran Classes in the UK <span class="go">→</span></a>
      <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/locations/usa/">Online Quran Classes in the USA <span class="go">→</span></a>
      <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/locations/canada/">Online Quran Classes in Canada <span class="go">→</span></a>
      <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/locations/australia/">Online Quran Classes in Australia <span class="go">→</span></a>
      <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/locations/uae/">Online Quran Classes in the UAE <span class="go">→</span></a>
      <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/locations/qatar/">Online Quran Classes in Qatar <span class="go">→</span></a>
      <a href="https://quranlyhub.com/locations/saudi-arabia/">Online Quran Classes in Saudi Arabia <span class="go">→</span></a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Questions about our academy</h2>
    <details class="faq" open>
      <summary>What makes QuranlyHub different from other online Quran academies?</summary>
      <p>QuranlyHub only uses Ijazah-certified tutors, teaches every class 1-on-1 rather than in groups, and schedules 24/7 across every time zone — so families in the UK, USA, Canada, Australia, UAE, Qatar and Saudi Arabia can find a class time that genuinely fits their day.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Why was QuranlyHub founded?</summary>
      <p>QuranlyHub was built to give Muslim families a structured alternative to impersonal group classes and unverified freelance tutors, by pairing every student with a vetted, Ijazah-certified tutor inside a clear, progressive curriculum from Qaida through Hifz and Tafseer.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Does QuranlyHub check the background of its Quran tutors?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Every tutor is Ijazah-certified and vetted for both teaching ability and child safety before being matched with any student.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Which countries does QuranlyHub serve?</summary>
      <p>QuranlyHub teaches Muslim families across the United Kingdom, United States, Canada, Australia, United Arab Emirates, Qatar and Saudi Arabia, with scheduling available 24/7 across all time zones.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-band">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;">Meet your tutor with a free trial class</h2>
      <p class="narrow" style="margin:10px auto 0;">No registration fee. No credit card required. Just a real class with a certified tutor, so your family can decide for yourselves.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="https://quranlyhub.com/contact/">Book Your Free Trial Class</a>
      <p style="margin-top:16px;font-size:0.92rem;color:var(--ink-soft);">Prefer to ask first? Message us on WhatsApp: <a href="https://wa.me/923439486140" style="color:var(--teal);font-weight:600;">+92 343 9486140</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

